            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "summary",
      "title": "What we learned",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "list",
          "items": [
            "You can count in hundredths in decimal language (0.01, 0.02…) and in fraction language (one hundredth, two hundredths…). This is dual counting.",
            "Ten hundredths regroup to make one tenth.",
            "You can count in any multiple of hundredths and record it as an equation.",
            "You can count beyond one whole: 1.01, 1.02, 1.03… is the same as 101 hundredths, 102 hundredths…"
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "callout",
          "text": "A number can be said in more than one way: 0.25 is {zero point two five}, {25 hundredths}, or {2 tenths and 5 hundredths}."
        }
      ],
      "pics": [
        {
          "id": "decimal-place-value"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "flashcards": [
    {
      "front": "How do you write one hundredth as a decimal?",
      "back": "0.01"
    },
    {
      "front": "What is dual counting?",
      "back": "Counting hundredths in decimals and in fractions."
    },
    {
      "front": "Counting up in hundredths, what comes after 0.09?",
      "back": "0.1 (or 0.10).\n\nTen hundredths regroup to make one tenth."
    },
    {
      "front": "What is a multiple?",
      "back": "The result of multiplying a number by an integer.\n\n2 × 5 = 10, so 10 is a multiple of 2 and of 5."
    },
    {
      "front": "What is a fraction?",
      "back": "It shows us how many equal parts in a whole."
    },
    {
      "front": "Two ways to say 0.34?",
      "back": "“Zero point three four” or “34 hundredths”."
    },
    {
      "front": "Count in fives from 0.05: 0.05, 0.10, 0.15 … what are the next two?",
      "back": "0.20 and 0.25.\n\nFive hundredths, ten hundredths, fifteen hundredths, twenty hundredths, twenty five hundredths."
    },
    {
      "front": "Count on: 0.24 + 0.02 = ?",
      "back": "0.26\n\nThe inverse is 0.26 − 0.02 = 0.24."
    },
    {
      "front": "Write 40 hundredths as a decimal and as fractions.",
      "back": "0.4 (or 0.40), 40/100 or 4/10."
    },
    {
      "front": "Ways to describe 0.25?",
      "back": "Zero point two five, twenty five hundredths, two tenths and five hundredths."
    },
    {
      "front": "Write 1 and 7 hundredths as a decimal.",
      "back": "1.07\n\nAs a fraction it is 1 7/100, or 107/100."
    },
    {
      "front": "How many hundredths are in 1.07?",
      "back": "107 hundredths.\n\nOne whole is 100 hundredths, plus 7 hundredths."
    }
  ],
